<section class="contextual-region carousel-section layout-full-width carousel-section--gallery-only" id="venue-gallery" data-venue-section data-layout="layout--full" data-original-slides="5">
    <div class="inner inner-900 venue-overview__intro">
      <h2 class="venue-overview__title">About Preston North End Football Club</h2>
              <div class="venue-overview__content">
                      <p class="venue-overview__body">Deepdale is a prestigious footballing venue, home to Preston North End and steeped in history. The Lilywhites' home ground holds the privileged title of being the oldest professional footballing site in the world in continuous use.</p><p class="venue-overview__body">Whilst many clubs have moved locations over time, Preston North End have remained loyal to the turf in PR1 since 21st January 1875. In 2004, the famous 'The Splash' statue was built to honour Sir Tom Finney, the club's most iconic player, now proudly standing outside 'The Gentry Bar', PNE's new fan zone.</p>
                  </div>
      
